WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.070
Choose a seated or resting posture that can remain workable for a while.

2
00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:12.270
Let the body be alert enough to notice and supported enough that discomfort does not have to become the center of the practice.

3
00:00:19.738 --> 00:00:22.118
Select one simple sensory point.

4
00:00:23.818 --> 00:00:30.138
It might be breath at the nostrils, contact in one hand, pressure beneath the feet, or one steady sound.

5
00:00:31.838 --> 00:00:36.288
Choose something neutral or mildly pleasant rather than intense.

6
00:00:48.734 --> 00:00:50.894
Let this point become the home for attention.

7
00:00:52.594 --> 00:00:55.414
You are not trying to exclude the rest of experience.

8
00:00:57.114 --> 00:01:00.744
You are giving the mind one clear place to return.

9
00:01:16.302 --> 00:01:18.952
Notice the detail that is available now.

10
00:01:20.652 --> 00:01:24.492
At the nostrils, perhaps coolness, warmth, or movement.

11
00:01:26.192 --> 00:01:30.812
In a hand, perhaps pressure, tingling, temperature, or simple contact.

12
00:01:49.482 --> 00:01:52.282
Stay for one complete cycle of the sensation.

13
00:01:53.982 --> 00:01:58.312
If the point changes with breathing, follow one inhale and one exhale.

14
00:02:00.012 --> 00:02:03.212
If it is steadier, remain for the length of one natural breath.

15
00:02:18.769 --> 00:02:20.549
Attention will move.

16
00:02:22.249 --> 00:02:27.579
A sound, thought, feeling, or body sensation may become more compelling.

17
00:02:29.279 --> 00:02:33.019
The moment you know attention has moved is already a moment of awareness.

18
00:02:48.577 --> 00:02:54.507
Name the movement quietly if that helps: thinking, hearing, planning, remembering.

19
00:02:56.207 --> 00:03:00.767
Then let the label go and return to the chosen point without arguing with what appeared.

20
00:03:19.437 --> 00:03:21.537
Feel the next clear contact with the point.

21
00:03:23.237 --> 00:03:25.757
Returning does not need to be sharp or forceful.

22
00:03:27.457 --> 00:03:30.997
It can be like setting down a light object with care.

23
00:03:52.778 --> 00:03:57.878
For several breaths, practice this simple sequence: know the point, notice wandering, return.

24
00:03:59.578 --> 00:04:01.878
Success is not uninterrupted concentration.

25
00:04:03.578 --> 00:04:05.338
Success is an honest return.

26
00:04:33.342 --> 00:04:35.542
Perhaps attention stays for only a second.

27
00:04:37.242 --> 00:04:38.042
Begin again.

28
00:04:39.742 --> 00:04:41.142
Perhaps it stays longer.

29
00:04:42.842 --> 00:04:47.822
There is no need to hold it tightly or compare this moment with the previous one.

30
00:05:06.492 --> 00:05:11.132
Notice whether effort has gathered in the forehead, eyes, jaw, shoulders, or hands.

31
00:05:12.832 --> 00:05:16.482
Let unnecessary effort soften while keeping the chosen point clear.

32
00:05:35.151 --> 00:05:38.111
Now become curious about the beginning of each contact.

33
00:05:39.811 --> 00:05:42.771
Where does the next inhale first become knowable?

34
00:05:44.471 --> 00:05:46.411
When does pressure first register?

35
00:05:48.111 --> 00:05:50.031
Let freshness support attention.

36
00:06:11.812 --> 00:06:13.442
Then notice the ending.

37
00:06:15.142 --> 00:06:18.492
A sensation fades, changes, or gives way to another.

38
00:06:20.192 --> 00:06:24.592
The point is stable enough to return to and alive enough never to be exactly the same.

39
00:06:46.373 --> 00:06:51.643
If the chosen point becomes uncomfortable or emotionally charged, select another neutral anchor.

40
00:06:53.343 --> 00:06:57.973
Changing wisely is not failure.

41
00:06:59.673 --> 00:07:02.883
The practice is steady attention, not endurance.

42
00:07:21.553 --> 00:07:22.253
Return again.

43
00:07:23.953 --> 00:07:26.343
Let sounds remain in the background.

44
00:07:28.043 --> 00:07:29.943
Let thoughts pass through the wider field.

45
00:07:31.643 --> 00:07:34.693
Keep the point in the foreground without needing to push anything away.

46
00:08:02.697 --> 00:08:05.767
For the next five breaths, count only the returns.

47
00:08:07.467 --> 00:08:12.187
Each time attention comes home, recognize that movement with quiet appreciation.

48
00:08:13.887 --> 00:08:16.077
Begin at one again whenever needed.

49
00:08:44.081 --> 00:08:44.971
Release counting.

50
00:08:46.671 --> 00:08:50.401
Stay with the point for one final stretch, relaxed and interested.

51
00:08:52.101 --> 00:08:56.871
Notice not only the sensation but also the quality of attending to it.

52
00:09:18.652 --> 00:09:22.082
Let the focus widen to include the whole body and the room.

53
00:09:23.782 --> 00:09:26.162
The chosen point remains part of a larger field.

54
00:09:27.862 --> 00:09:32.532
Hear sounds, feel support, and notice light through open or closed eyes.

55
00:09:48.090 --> 00:09:50.660
Move fingers or shoulders if that feels useful.

56
00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:54.640
You practiced returning, not perfection.

57
00:09:56.340 --> 00:10:00.000
That same return can be available during the next ordinary task.
